:null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":283518839,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM1MTg4Mzk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","color":"ffddff","default":true,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-05-24T05:51:41Z","updated_at":"2025-05-29T15:48:01Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.4.1 stable\n\n### System information\n\nSteam Runtime 2 (soldier) 2 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 970 (nvidia) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-7600K CPU @ 3.80GHz (4 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf you follow the steps to reproduce and run the project, you will see that ```after``` is printed, even though it comes after ```if false:```. My assumption as to what is happening is that the ```@warning_ignore(...)``` is being treated as if it's on a new line. I'm not sure if this is a bug or how this should be interpreted but this issue came up while testing a plugin which inlines as much as possible in scripts. Both ```@warning_ignore_start(...)``` and ```@warning_ignore_restore(...)``` throw errors in this scenario which do not allow anything to come after them on the same line so maybe this logic should also be applied to ```@warning_ignore(...)``` as well.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAttach the following script to a node and run the project:\n```\nextends Node\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tif false: print(\"before\"); @warning_ignore(\"incompatible_ternary\") print(\"after\")\n```\nStill happens if you remove the ```print(\"before\");```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106764/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106764/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}